roup intervals below parity, none above, five overlapping. Across all 192 groups: 66 below, 17 above, 109 overlapping. All 17 above-parity intervals are bypass/reused controls. Intervals are not multiplicity-adjusted and do not establish universal effects. Memory improvements relative to v1 and remaining baseline costs are both retained in the evidence.","limits":"V2 changes the crossover, dispatch and temporary lifetime together; this is not a factorial attribution experiment. No new full crate/debug/state-history/concurrency/internal-unreduced-storage/quotient timing/representative application-size qualification is claimed. No theorem that every three-product implementation is unsuitable follows.","next":"Resume the remaining original source audit, starting with Arb dot-product and error-bound support. The wide common-scale idea may be revisited for a measured application that predominantly reaches it, but do not keep iterating generic dispatch variants without new workload evidence. All original references and full inventory reconciliation remain in scope."},"limits":"Same finite release oracle and benchmark corpus as v1; old baseline numerical/memory/trace evidence and four exact binaries are reused, while all CPU/allocation baseline measurements are fresh. No new full crate/debug/state-history/concurrency/internal-unreduced-storage/quotient timing/application-size/WASM/other-architecture qualification. Paired per-group bootstrap intervals are not multiplicity-adjusted. Source copy and dedicated executable sizes do not bound build-cache growth or RSS. Earlier failed gates remain preserved.","production":"No live or donor source change. All 955 live hashes remain at the four retained continuation transfers. No cleanup, deletion, commit, push or external report."}
